From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:36:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Describe the CPU PMU

Describe one PMU for both T8132 clusters on the P-cluster PMU FIQ, as
"arm64: dts: apple: t6040, t8140: Describe one CPU PMU per SoC" does.
The AIC driver raises the PMU FIQ of either cluster as AIC_CPU_PMU_P, so
drop the per-cluster AIC affinities: with them that interrupt, and with
it the PMU's supported CPUs, would cover the P cores only. Nothing else
uses the PMU FIQ indices.

The node is disabled: the M4 event table is measured on T6040 and T8140
cores, not yet on T8132. A board enables it once that measurement passes.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 21 +++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index d6a01e1473..efd84b8c9d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -493,18 +493,6 @@
 			      <0x3 0x81040000 0x0 0x4000>;
 			reg-names = "core", "event";
 			power-domains = <&ps_aic>;
-
-			affinities {
-				e-core-pmu-affinity {
-					apple,fiq-index = <AIC_CPU_PMU_E>;
-					cpus = <&cpu_e0 &cpu_e1 &cpu_e2 &cpu_e3 &cpu_e4 &cpu_e5>;
-				};
-
-				p-core-pmu-affinity {
-					apple,fiq-index = <AIC_CPU_PMU_P>;
-					cpus = <&cpu_p0 &cpu_p1 &cpu_p2 &cpu_p3>;
-				};
-			};
 		};
 
 		nub_spmi: spmi@0 {
@@ -914,6 +902,15 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	cpu_pmu: pmu {
+		compatible = "apple,t8132-pmu";
+		interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+		/* The AIC raises both clusters' PMU FIQs as this one. */
+		interrupts = <AIC_FIQ AIC_CPU_PMU_P IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+		/* Enabled per board once the T8132 event placement is measured. */
+		status = "disabled";
+	};
+
 	timer {
 		compatible = "arm,armv8-timer";
 		interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
